aphify_skill_step6_obsidian_html", "label": "Step 6: Obsidian Vault + HTML Export", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_step9_cleanup", "label": "Step 9: Save Manifest, Update Cost Tracker, Cleanup", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_honesty_rules", "label": "Honesty Rules", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never invent an edge (use AMBIGUOUS if unsure); never skip the corpus-size check warning; always show token cost in the report; never hide cohesion scores behind symbols; never run HTML viz on a graph with more than 5,000 nodes without warning the user. These rules keep the extraction pipeline auditable and trustworthy."}, {"id": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_shrink_guard", "label": "Graph Shrink Guard (#479)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "to_json() refuses to write graph.json when the newly built graph has fewer nodes than the existing one (#479), preventing a bad or partial extraction from silently clobbering a good graph. GRAPH_REPORT.md and the analysis sidecar are written only after a successful (non-shrinking) export, so they never describe a graph that graph.json doesn't actually contain."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_graphify_command", "target": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_step1_ensure_installed", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "c